# ===== Separate concurrent session's work: not part of this commit =====
# A different, concurrent Claude Code session (see OVERNIGHT_B9_EXTERNAL_STATUS.md
# at repo root, written by that session) is running/has run a large B9/B3
# seed-landscape sweep (PHM2010 D1/D2/D3 + NASA N1-N4, 700+ runs, still growing
# as of this .gitignore edit) inside this Chinese-named diagnostic tree, under
# its own separate user instructions -- deliberately kept out of this English-
# named methods/ framework. That status doc itself asks for user confirmation
# before committing/pushing. Whole directory excluded wholesale (rather than
# per-subdirectory) since it is still actively being extended; the user should
# review and decide what (if anything) to commit from it separately from this
# task's own work.
/05_统计检验/seed_statistics/
/shared/reproducibility/build_phm_task_frozen_preprocess.py
/shared/reproducibility/PHM2010_D2_frozen_preprocess/
/shared/reproducibility/PHM2010_D3_frozen_preprocess/
/shared/reproducibility/NASA_N*_frozen_preprocess/
/shared/reproducibility/build_nasa_task_frozen_preprocess.py
/OVERNIGHT_B9_EXTERNAL_STATUS.md
/MTW_TASK_AUDIT.md
/NASA_TASK_AUDIT.md

# ===== Python / OS cruft =====
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ===== Raw PHM2010 dataset (18GB+, fetched via scripts/download_phm2010.py) =====
# The small DERIVED feature file data/PHM2010/features/run_level_features_all.csv
# (5.4MB, irreproducible from a lost original extraction script per
# baselines/htt_net/README.md, no license issue) is deliberately NOT excluded here
# and IS committed -- see data/README.md.
/data/PHM2010/raw/

# ===== Training checkpoints / large binaries (regenerable by rerunning a method) =====
# Default --save-checkpoint is "none"; even when a user opts into saving them,
# they must never be committed.
**/*.pth
**/*.pt
**/*.pkl
**/*.ckpt

# ===== Smoke-test scratch output (never mixed into results/) =====
/tmp/

# ===== Formal per-seed run artifacts under results/ =====
# Only small aggregated summary/*.csv files are committed -- see RESULTS_POLICY.md
# "What gets committed to git". Per-seed predictions/logs/configs stay local.
/results/PHM2010/*/*/seed*/

# ===== Credentials =====
.env
*.kaggle.json
kaggle.json
.kaggle/

# ===== Per-method preprocessing caches (regenerable, machine-local) =====
# Several methods cache derived windows/images on first use (e.g.
# methods/B5_MultiSource_Attention/_cache/, methods/data/PHM2010/cache/) --
# never the raw dataset itself, always a regenerable intermediate.
**/_cache/
**/cache/
**/*.npy
**/*.npz
